[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 395,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 228,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58167,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 22,
        "headingId": 228,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Elastofibroma is a benign, ill-defined proliferation of fibroelastic tissue with excessive abnormal elastic fibres.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:15:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 396,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 229,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58168,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 22,
        "headingId": 229,
        "headingText": "<p>8820/0 Elastofibroma</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-01-31T09:22:31"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 397,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 230,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58169,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 22,
        "headingId": 230,
        "headingText": "<p>FB51.Y &amp; XH3BQ8 Other specified fibroblastic disorders &amp; Elastofibroma</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-01-23T16:06:45"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 398,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 231,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58170,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 22,
        "headingId": 231,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> elastofibroma dorsi.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:15:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 399,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 232,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58171,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 22,
        "headingId": 232,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:15:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 400,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 233,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58172,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 22,
        "headingId": 233,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Elastofibroma most often arises in the deep soft tissue between the lower scapula and the thoracic wall. It may rarely occur in extrascapular locations, including other parts of the thoracic wall, extremities, limb girdles, neck, eyes, and gastrointestinal tract or other viscera. Although elastofibroma is usually a unilateral and solitary mass, bilateral or multiple lesions have been reported.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:15:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 401,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 234,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58173,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 22,
        "headingId": 234,
        "headingText": "<p>Elastofibroma occurs almost exclusively in the elderly, with a peak incidence between the seventh and eighth decades of life. There is a striking female predominance (M:F&nbsp;ratio: ~0.08:1) {7116305}. The lesion usually presents as a slow-growing asymptomatic mass or rarely causes pain, stiffness, scapular snapping, and impingement. CT and MRI show a poorly defined, heterogeneous soft tissue mass with tissue attenuation similar to that of skeletal muscle interlaced with fat strands {8751681}. The lesion may be hypermetabolic on FDG&nbsp;PET-CT {20978756}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-02-10T09:34:52"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 402,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 235,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58174,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 22,
        "headingId": 235,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Although elastofibroma was previously considered to be rare, its exact prevalence is unknown. The lesions are detectable in 2% of adults aged &gt;&nbsp;60&nbsp;years by CT and in 16% of autopsy cases from adults aged &gt;&nbsp;55&nbsp;years {9762978; 1124654}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:15:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 403,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 236,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58175,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 22,
        "headingId": 236,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:15:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 404,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 237,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58176,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 22,
        "headingId": 237,
        "headingText": "<p>Elastotic degeneration of collagen or abnormal elastotic fibrogenesis may underlie the pathogenesis of elastofibroma {13916810; 1842374; 3552953}, and active neovascularization or endothelial&ndash;mesenchymal transition plays a potential pathogenetic role {19132384; 25820560}. Elastofibroma often exhibits chromosomal instability including gains of 6p25-q25 and Xq12-q22 and losses of 1p, 13q, 19p, and 22q {12165800; 20422214}. Deletions of <em>CASR</em> (3q13.33-q21.1), <em>GSTP1</em> (11q13.2), and <em>BRCA2</em> (13q13.1), as well as gains of <em>APC</em> (5q22.2) and <em>PAH</em> (12q23.2), have also been described {20422214}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-02-10T09:36:13"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 411,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 244,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58177,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 22,
        "headingId": 244,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The lesion is poorly defined and rubbery, composed of grey or whitish fibrous tissue with variable intervening streaks of yellow fatty tissue. The diameter ranges from 2 to 15&nbsp;cm.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:15:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 405,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 238,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58178,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 22,
        "headingId": 238,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Elastofibroma is composed predominantly of fibrocollagenous tissue containing a large number of abnormal elastic fibres and dispersed, bland-appearing spindle cells, admixed with a variable amount of adipose tissue and small blood vessels. A focally myxoid matrix is common. The elastic fibres are typically thick or coarse, deeply eosinophilic, and fragmented into linearly arranged globular or serrated disc-like structures, simulating beads on a string, which are highlighted using elastic stains.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:15:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 406,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 239,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58179,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 22,
        "headingId": 239,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Linear (braid-like), globular, or stellate structures of degenerated elastic fibres are cytological features in elastofibroma {14648789}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:15:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 407,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 240,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58180,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 22,
        "headingId": 240,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:15:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 410,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 243,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58181,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 22,
        "headingId": 243,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> a bland-appearing, hypocellular fibrofatty tumour with excessive abnormal elastic fibres.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:15:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 408,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 241,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58182,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 22,
        "headingId": 241,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:15:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 409,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 242,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58183,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 22,
        "headingId": 242,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Elastofibroma is a benign lesion and is cured by simple excision. Local recurrence is exceptional.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:15:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]